---
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const host = site.url.replace('https://', '');
---
<p>
  This is the privacy policy for <a href={site.url}>{host}</a>, run by {site.legalName}. It is short because
  the site does very little with your data.
</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>The site has no accounts, forms, cookies, or analytics. Fonts and scripts are served from our own domain.</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>If you visit.</strong> Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs: IP address, browser, pages
    requested, and the time. We use them only to keep the site running and secure.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>If you email us.</strong> We receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it to reply,
    and if we go on to work together, to run that engagement.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>That is all. We do not buy, sell, or combine data about you from anywhere else.</p>

<h2>Who else sees it</h2>
<p>
  The companies that host the site and our email, to the extent they need to in order to provide those
  services. Nobody else, unless the law requires it. Those providers may store data outside the UAE; where they
  do, we rely on their contractual safeguards.
</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
  Server logs are kept for a short period and then deleted. Email is kept for as long as we are in contact and
  for the period our accounting and legal obligations require.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to our using it.
  Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond. We are a UAE company and work under
  UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data. You can complain to the UAE Data
  Office if you think we have got something wrong.
</p>

<h2>Two other things</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Information on this site is general. It is not advice for your situation, and we may change it without notice.</li>
  <li>Our consulting and engineering work is governed by the contract we sign with each client, not by this page.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>
  If we add analytics, a contact form, or anything else that changes what we collect, we will update this page
  and the date at the top before it goes live.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
  {site.legalName}, {site.address.lines[0]}, {site.address.lines[1]}.
  Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
</p>
